// States on 1925-01-01: how the provinces of assets/map/provinces.ron group into the states of
// the simulation. Read by `bf-mapgen`; rules and approximations: docs/map-pipeline.pt-BR.md,
// "Estados".
//
// - `states`: explicit states, applied first. A selector is a province key (Natural Earth
//   `adm1_code`, carve key `<from>~<suffix>`, `ADM0-<A3>`) or an ISO 3166-2 code, which takes every
//   province with that code (Natural Earth splits some ISO units, e.g. IE-D, PH-MNL).
// - `countries`: rule per Natural Earth `adm0_a3` for the provinces left over.
//   `Admin1`: one state per admin-1 unit (key `<A3>-<ISO suffix>`).
//   `Whole(name, key)`: the whole unit is one state; units with the same key form one state, and a
//   key equal to an explicit state's joins it.
//   `Field(field, names)`: one state per value of `region` or `region_sub`; `names` renames values
//   and values renamed alike merge.
//   Units without a rule give one state per province.
// - `attach`: islets and fragments that join the state of another province.
// - `tiny`: states allowed to have no pixel.
// A group that would mix owners, or colonies and metropole, is split by bf-mapgen (the largest
// part keeps the key); carved provinces are states of their own unless listed here.
(
    start_date: "1925-01-01",
    states: [
        // ---------------------------------------------------------------- British Isles
        (key: "IRL-LEINSTER", name: "Leinster", provinces: ["IE-D", "IE-KE", "IE-MH", "IE-LH", "IE-WH", "IE-OY", "IE-LS", "IE-LD", "IE-KK", "IE-CW", "IE-WX", "IE-WW"]),
